# Parametria run artifacts (issue #9). The `parametria` agent preset's persona
# instructs every run to keep its screenshots, spec dumps and generator scripts
# in `.parametria-evidence/<session id>/`, and its uv cache in `.uv-cache/` —
# both resolved against the session workspace, which IS this repository whenever
# a run is driven from here (all three harvested runs were). These entries are
# not decoration: without them the persona's own instructions dirty the tracked
# surface. Note what they do and do not cover — they contain the artifacts of a
# run that FOLLOWS the persona. The loose `cabinet-*.png` / `spec.json` litter
# that prompted this came from runs with no such instruction, and those names
# match nothing here: a run that ignores the persona stays exactly as visible in
# `git status` as it was before.
# `dsh-preset-parametria/tests/evidence-hygiene.test.mjs` DERIVES this list from
# the persona text, so a persona naming a new DOT-PREFIXED workspace directory
# fails the gate until that directory is ignored here. A name without the
# leading dot is not separable from prose and stays a review question; the fence
# documents that limit rather than implying it covers everything.
.parametria-evidence/
.uv-cache/
